WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.680
Nasal messenger RNA drops restored youthful memory in aging mice without removing Alzheimer plaques. This is Longevity Weekly Episode 10. The science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice. After that mouse result, the week moves through anti-protazole treatment records, a microbe made NAD precursor, a weighted vest in a diet study, an early Alzheimer imaging, then-inflammaging. University of Sydney researchers in work science daily describes

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.640
from advanced science, packed messenger RNA into lipid nanoparticles, and put it in the

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.320
noses of mice so local cells would manufacture brain-derived neurotrophic factor.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.920
That protein helps neuron survive, form connections, and change as memories are stored.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:51.200
In the aged animals, learning and memory rows until performance look like the younger groups.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:56.600
Mice bred to develop Alzheimer's disease were kept from the severe memory drop the model

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.540
usually produces.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.400
purposes. Professor Greg Neely at the Charles Perkins Center has said a human trial could

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.800
test whether the nose offers a non-invasive path around the blood brain barrier. No such

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:13.380
trial is reported here. The team also lists stroke, traumatic brain injury, and rare genetic

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.860
conditions as later possibilities, which is a hope, not a finding in people.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:24.980
Fight aging describes an observational comparison, not a randomized aging trial, in people treated

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.100
for protozoan infection versus people who were not treated.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.640
The drugs are those used against toxoplasma Gandhi, which causes toxoplasmosis and against

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:35.720
other protozoa.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.480
Treated people showed surprisingly large reductions in disease risk and immortality.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:46.000
The commentary says the gap is big enough to take seriously and also says healthier, more

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.520
active, or more medically savvy people may simply be the ones who got the drugs.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.960
One reading is that toxoplasmosis harms people whose immune systems are otherwise normal.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.120
Another is that the drugs themselves do something useful.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.280
Because treatment in those people is usually short, a lasting effect on the pace of aging

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:05.900
is treated as the weaker reading.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.660
These sources do not establish approval of anti-protazole drugs for any aging-related use.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:17.890
A laboratory study summarized by fight aging from science advances found that some gut microbes,

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:24.650
probes, including particular probiotic species, make amide and methyl nicotinamide, or NMNA.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:30.710
Human intestinal cells, and cells from fruit flies and mice, took that molecule up and folded

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.770
it into NAD redox reactions.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.050
NAD is the coenzyme mitochondria need.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.890
People with gut dysbiosis and inflammation had less of it in stool, which is an association

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:45.150
not a demonstration that the missing molecule caused the illness.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:51.950
In mice, giving NMNA throughout the body promoted intestinal stem cell regeneration and repair

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:52.830
of the gut lining.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:58.290
Work in Drosophila implicated CERT-1, an enzyme that consumes NAD.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:04.190
The paper says conversion to NAD-plus runs through the price handler pathway, not the

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:08.530
salvage pathway, and that the molecule brings a methyl group into the host cell.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:14.010
The same commentary says clinical evidence for material benefits from Vitamin B3 derived

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:21.950
NAD precursors in specific conditions is poor, and that those precursors do not raise NAD as well as exercise does.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:26.670
Approval of those precursors for an aging-related use is not established here.

00:03:27.711 --> 00:03:32.491
Ecoportal reports a human diet comparison, not a lifespan trial, in older adults.

00:03:33.251 --> 00:03:39.131
People who wore a two-pound vest, with plates added each week, barely changed their resting energy burn.

00:03:39.731 --> 00:03:42.891
People who dieted without the vest saw that burn fall hard.

00:03:42.891 --> 00:03:48.071
The result is about resting metabolism during weight loss, not about disease or years

00:03:48.071 --> 00:03:48.651
of life.

00:03:49.071 --> 00:03:52.551
A vest in a study is not a regulator-reviewed treatment for aging.

00:03:53.626 --> 00:03:58.246
Fight aging describes imaging in people during the long early phase of Alzheimer's disease,

00:03:58.646 --> 00:04:02.966
when symptoms are still mild and easy to confuse with ordinary cognitive aging.

00:04:03.466 --> 00:04:07.826
The hippocampus, the memory center that draws most of the attention, is not where tissue

00:04:07.826 --> 00:04:13.486
loss first becomes visible on scans. The amygdala and the enterrhynal cortex thin earlier,

00:04:13.946 --> 00:04:18.866
while biochemical and structural change is already building. Whether acting in that window,

00:04:19.146 --> 00:04:24.066
with tools available now, can delay or prevent later disease is not settled by this report.

00:04:25.215 --> 00:04:30.795
Inflamaging, this week's mechanism is chronic sterile low-grade inflammation that rises with age

00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:37.295
when there is no fresh infection and no fresh injury. And a 2026 human cohort shows how

00:04:37.295 --> 00:04:44.375
slippery the age signal is, among 153 treatment naive patients with six kinds of cancer, split

00:04:44.375 --> 00:04:51.335
at age 60, tumor mutational burden sat higher in the older group, a median of 4.55 mutations

00:04:51.335 --> 00:04:57.915
per megabase against 2.84, whole genome sequencing supplied that burden and the fraction of the genome

00:04:57.915 --> 00:05:04.055
that was altered, RNA sequencing and proteomics scored inflammatory pathways in paired tumor

00:05:04.055 --> 00:05:10.535
and normal tissue. A 2007 perspective in mechanisms of aging and development treated much of

00:05:10.535 --> 00:05:16.355
the aging phenotype, immunosenscence included, as an imbalance between inflammatory networks

00:05:16.355 --> 00:05:22.595
and anti-inflammatory ones. Lifelong antigens and damaging agents keep the pro-inflammatory side

00:05:22.595 --> 00:05:27.835
busy. On that view, a long healthy life would need both a quieter inflammatory response

00:05:27.835 --> 00:05:33.275
and anti-inflammatory networks strong enough to cancel the load. When the balance fails,

00:05:33.275 --> 00:05:36.255
trials, frailty, and ordinary age-related disease follow.

00:05:36.715 --> 00:05:41.415
The authors said the evidence they were drawing on came largely from people, and they framed

00:05:41.415 --> 00:05:44.175
the problem as a whole system rather than one switch.

00:05:44.555 --> 00:05:50.455
A 2014 report from a National Institute on Aging Session in the Journals of Gerontology,

00:05:50.755 --> 00:05:56.115
Series A, called this pattern a highly significant risk factor for illness and death in older

00:05:56.115 --> 00:06:00.915
adults, because most age-related diseases share an inflammatory pathogenesis.

00:06:00.915 --> 00:06:06.315
It also said the exact cause, and any proof that the inflammation itself produces the

00:06:06.315 --> 00:06:08.835
bad outcomes, was still largely unknown.

00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:14.435
The session's job was to name the pathways that set inflammation across organs, not to

00:06:14.435 --> 00:06:15.075
close the case.

00:06:15.715 --> 00:06:20.215
A 2018 review in Nature Review's Endocrinology described the inputs.

00:06:20.775 --> 00:06:26.275
A small set of innate immune receptors reads many signals, pathogens labeled non-self,

00:06:26.275 --> 00:06:31.115
cell debris and molecules sitting in the wrong place labeled self, nutrients

00:06:31.115 --> 00:06:36.795
and gut microbes labeled quasi-self, metaflimation, the inflammation that comes with metabolic

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:41.215
disease and too much nutrient intake, was said to use the same machinery.

00:06:41.895 --> 00:06:46.895
Microbes matter to both because they release inflammatory products, join circadian rhythms,

00:06:47.475 --> 00:06:48.615
and talk to other organs.

00:06:49.155 --> 00:06:52.835
The review argued that chronic disease is not only a result of aging.

00:06:52.835 --> 00:06:59.115
It can speed aging and look like aging that arrived early. DNA methylation, glycomics,

00:06:59.315 --> 00:07:04.415
metabolomics, and lipidomics were offered as ways to tell biological age from the birth

00:07:04.415 --> 00:07:10.035
day in metabolic disease. That is a measurement proposal, not a test already tied to lifespan.

00:07:10.715 --> 00:07:16.815
The 2026 study in Immunal Oncology Technology asked which of those age patterns survive

00:07:16.815 --> 00:07:22.475
once cancer type is accounted for. The age groups did not carry the same cancers, so the

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:25.175
The main links were rerun in multi-variable models.

00:07:25.675 --> 00:07:30.775
Most of the age-associated molecular differences were substantially explained by cancer type.

00:07:31.215 --> 00:07:35.995
What held was an age-related increase in normal tissue inflammation at the protein level,

00:07:36.415 --> 00:07:44.315
and a larger tumor versus normal inflammation jump in MSI-high tumors, plus 0.065, P equal

00:07:44.315 --> 00:07:49.135
to 0.015, and plus 0.087 after adjustment.

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:54.295
Normal tissue inflammation tracked with the paired tumors mutational burden at the protein

00:07:54.295 --> 00:07:58.235
level, spearmen RS equal to 0.387.

00:07:58.655 --> 00:08:03.855
The authors say that correlation is not evidence that body-wide inflomaging drove the genomic

00:08:03.855 --> 00:08:04.535
instability.

00:08:05.175 --> 00:08:12.395
Inflammation scored inside the tumor did not track mutational burden, RS equal to 0.07, P equal

00:08:12.395 --> 00:08:19.415
to 0.54. Berberine, an alkaloid from Berberus species and from Coptus genesis, is the

00:08:19.415 --> 00:08:25.415
intervention a 2026 Fittoterapia review puts against several of these processes. The

00:08:25.415 --> 00:08:30.655
review is mechanism writing from cells and animals, not a randomized human trial of aging.

00:08:31.235 --> 00:08:37.115
It describes activation of AMP activated protein kinase through mild inhibition of mitochondrial

00:08:37.115 --> 00:08:43.675
complex-1, which can suppress m-tore-linked building pathways, increase autophagy and mitophagy,

00:08:44.015 --> 00:08:47.015
and help clear damaged mitochondria and clumped proteins.

00:08:47.735 --> 00:08:49.935
Respiratory efficiency is said to improve.

00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:55.735
Pathological reactive oxygen species are limited while ordinary redox signaling stays.

00:08:56.455 --> 00:08:59.175
Antioxidant defenses rise through NRF-2.

00:08:59.175 --> 00:09:07.535
N.F. Kappa-B is kept from moving into the nucleus and transcription of T.N.F. Alpha, IL-6, and IL-1 beta

00:09:07.535 --> 00:09:14.015
falls. The review calls the compound xenomorphic. It may quiet the senescence-associated secretory

00:09:14.015 --> 00:09:20.875
phenotype without killing cells broadly, partly by changing P-16 and cyclin expression. These sources

00:09:20.875 --> 00:09:27.455
do not establish approval of burberine for any aging-related use, and the review flags pharmacokinetic problems

00:09:27.455 --> 00:09:32.595
and safety questions. What remains open is the jump from a shared inflammatory signature

00:09:32.595 --> 00:09:39.095
to a cause of aging that a treatment can safely cut. The 2014 session left cause and causality

00:09:39.095 --> 00:09:44.355
unresolved. The cancer cohort shows an age gap that is mostly a mix of diseases gap.

00:09:44.995 --> 00:09:50.095
The pattern sits on the hallmark of chronic inflammation. The limit the cancer author's state is

00:09:50.095 --> 00:09:55.495
the one to keep. Inflamed normal tissue tracking with tumor mutational burden does not mean

00:09:55.495 --> 00:09:58.075
Inflammaging is what destabilized the genome.

00:09:58.515 --> 00:10:04.075
It is worth knowing that a large observational link in people between antiprotosol treatment

00:10:04.075 --> 00:10:07.875
and later disease or death can still be a record of who received care.

00:10:08.415 --> 00:10:13.975
Holding resting burned steady with a light vest, in a human diet comparison speaks to metabolism

00:10:13.975 --> 00:10:16.715
during weight loss and not to extra years of life.

00:10:17.355 --> 00:10:22.195
Imaging an early Alzheimer's disease puts tissue loss in the amygdala and enterrhynal cortex

00:10:22.195 --> 00:10:23.575
before the hippocampus.

00:10:23.575 --> 00:10:28.875
So, the memory center is a later chapter, and a higher mutational burden in older cancer

00:10:28.875 --> 00:10:31.795
patients can still be mostly which cancers were in the room.

